 After the parent explicitly releases execution, the intended invocation is:
 
 ```text
-python3 -I -B artifacts/verification/io-lifecycle-harness-probes/run_probes.py attempt01 --parent-released
+python3 -I -S -B artifacts/verification/io-lifecycle-harness-probes/revisions/02/run_probes.py attempt01 --parent-released
 ```
 
 The release flag is an assertion of prior parent authorization, not authorization itself. Do not invoke it while the hold remains. This first probe suite may expose fixture or harness errors; preserve the result and distinguish such errors from the intended fault before revising sources. Additional lifecycle driver/service/capacity/revision cases still wait for current-source smoke evidence.
 
 Limits: no hardware, native endpoint, model, OS driver/service effect, live tree mutation or acquired program execution. No hard filesystem quota, hard SQLite timing bound, hostile-code sandbox, whole-host attestation or guaranteed finalization after SIGKILL/host/storage failure. Selected external package/interpreter/SQLite manifests and actual origin receipts do not attest all caches, stdlib or shared libraries. The source-copy boundary is the already retained full696/provider146-derived snapshot05, not current live public-I/O compatibility.
+
+Revision02 preserves the original root preparation and its `b787109b...` manifest. It adds an executing/retained outer-harness before/after identity gate, exactly13 closed result counts, and `-I -S -B` startup for the outer launcher and runner wrappers. The explicitly selected installed validation roots and six metadata hashes are retained in `approved-external-roots.json`; this metadata acquisition did not import the selected packages. The post-capture close-failure probe now asserts one actual inner unittest cleanup error and retains that traceback, while preserving the earlier logical snapshot and changed raw database. These remain unexecuted source corrections.
